  "id": "aggregation-problems",
  "term": "aggregation problems",
  "definition": "Aggregation problems are distortions or errors that can arise when researchers group information into larger contextual units, such as communities or neighborhoods, because different ways of drawing those boundaries can change the results. In this sense, the problem comes from the subjective choice of how separate observations are combined into a single area.",
